The prefix length of the segment the nodes share, which the addresses drawn
from this network are configured with, as `64`.

When not set, it is the prefix length of the address of the node on the
segment, the one whose prefix holds the range of the network: a node with an
address `fd01:2345:6789:2902::11/64` configures the addresses drawn from
`fd01:2345:6789:2902::5:0/120` with `/64`. Set it when the nodes have no
address on the segment, as on a segment dedicated to the addresses of the
services.
